{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And what does He rage — HaShem has not raged.</b> That the Holy One, blessed be He, was not angry all those days — and that is what the prophet said to Israel: ״My people, remember now what Balak counseled״ etc., as is found in tractate Berakhot. And we say there: and how long is His rage? A moment. And how long is a moment? Like its utterance. The difficulty: how could he curse them in such a brief moment? And one may answer that he was able to say all of them. And thus it is written: ״ויהפוך ה' אלהיך לך את הקללה לברכה״ — that HaShem your Elohim turned for you the curse into a blessing — ״שאמר ותרועת מלך בו״ — the king's shout is in it. He turned all of them. However, it is difficult from what we say there: that heretic who was in the neighborhood of Rabbi Yehoshua ben Levi, who used to torment him greatly etc. — when that moment arrived, he dozed off; ״thus you learn that it is not the way of the world to do thus, as it is written: גם ענוש לצדיק לא טוב — even to strike a righteous man is not good,״ and even to a heretic.״ And how could he curse him in that moment? And what curse could he say in such a brief moment? One must say that the matter depends only on beginning the curse at the time of rage. And so too it is proven there, for it concludes: Rabbi Yehoshua said — from the blessings of that wicked man you learn what was in his heart: he sought to say ״let them not have synagogues,״ as I will explain below. And all these curses he could not have said in that moment, but ״thus you learn that the matter depends on the beginning.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The verse quoted in the Gemara is Judges 5:23; the biblical text reads מארת מלך, but the Gemara's reading ותרועת מלך is preserved here as in the Talmudic source. The phrase שאמר ותרועת מלך בו is the Gemara's exegesis connecting Deuteronomy 23:6 to Judges 5:23."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:08.748399067Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}